id=a52sxq_devicecare_sleep_lists
name=Device Care: list every restrictable app in the sleeping app lists
author=kusti420
description=Battery > Background usage limits > Sleeping / Deep sleeping / Never auto sleeping apps > Add only offered apps for which SemAppRestrictionManager.canRestrict() is true. For the deep sleep type that check also applies Samsung's server-pushed deep sleep policy (ScpmPolicyForDeepSleep) and a usage-based MARs filter chain, so apps like Clock, Good Lock and its modules, Gallery or Google Photos never appeared even though the framework's own protection check (canRestrictWithReason) has no objection. The Add lists now use canRestrictWithReason and ignore only its widget (0x8) and quick panel tile (0x100000) bits, as Device Care already does elsewhere. Hard protections stay: system apps, default keyboard/launcher/SMS/phone apps, device admins, the active wallpaper, AOD clock, protected and important-role packages. MARs still applies its usage filters when a restriction is set, and Device Care's automatic features keep using canRestrict.
